{
  "title": "LUXR",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "The LUXR drum",
        "machine (M-VAVE FM-1",
        "firmware) as a sound",
        "generator: eight",
        "drum voices after",
        "the Sonic Potions",
        "LXR, each a synth",
        "layer and a sample",
        "layer, with drive,",
        "delay, reverb, a",
        "master filter, a",
        "compressor and a",
        "limiter.",
        "",
        "Move sequences it:",
        "put LUXR on a drum",
        "track and play the",
        "pads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pads",
      "lines": [
        "Note map MOVE:",
        "Pads 1-8 (notes",
        "36-43): Kick, Snare,",
        "Clap, Cl Hat,",
        "Op Hat, Tom, Rim,",
        "Cymbal.",
        "Pads 9-16 (44-51):",
        "nothing.",
        "Velocity over 110",
        "accents.",
        "",
        "Note map GM: General",
        "MIDI drum notes.",
        "Note map TONAL:",
        "every note plays",
        "Tonal Snd, C3 its",
        "own pitch.",
        "",
        "The closed hat",
        "chokes the open one.",
        "",
        "Setup > MIDI Ch:",
        "All - every channel",
        "the slot passes on.",
        "1-16 - only that",
        "channel plays LUXR."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Knobs & Shift",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Knob pages",
          "lines": [
            "LUXR (first page):",
            "1 Volume  2 Tune",
            "3 Decay   4 Filter",
            "5 Reso    6 Drive",
            "7 Delay return",
            "8 Reverb return",
            "",
            "Sounds: hit a pad -",
            "its sound's pages",
            "open (that one",
            "only).",
            "Page 1: synth layer",
            "1 Pitch 2 Decay",
            "3-7 LUXR's EDIT 3-7",
            "8 Drive",
            "(Perform shows each",
            "sound's own names.)",
            "Page 2: sample layer",
            "Page 3: Level Pan",
            "Delay Reverb | Drive",
            "Attack Gate Release",
            "Page 4: LFO 1 | 2",
            "Page 5: WAV File,",
            "Length, Variation",
            "",
            "Shift + knob: fine."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Perform",
          "lines": [
            "LUXR page > Perform:",
            "the knobs as on",
            "LUXR, a row and its",
            "SHIFT row.",
            "",
            "Knob 1-8: row A",
            "Shift+knob: row B",
            "Jog: the sound",
            "Jog click: layer",
            "Pad: its sound",
            "Touch knob: value",
            "Back: out",
            "",
            "SOUND: synth layer",
            "Shift: sample layer",
            "MIX: Level Pan Dly",
            "Rev Drv Atk Gate Rel",
            "Shift: LFO 1 + 2",
            "KIT: Vol Tune Decay",
            "Filt Reso Drive",
            "Dly Rev returns",
            "Shift: Dly time",
            "Fdbk Size Damp",
            "Thresh Ratio",
            "Makeup Limiter"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pages",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Kits",
          "lines": [
            "The preset browser:",
            "the 13 LUXR preset",
            "patches, Factory,",
            "then your own kits.",
            "Patch 1 loads when",
            "LUXR starts.",
            "",
            "Setup > Save Kit:",
            "type a name - the",
            "kit is saved and",
            "listed. Delete Kit",
            "removes the loaded",
            "kit of yours.",
            "Kits of your own are",
            "kept in UserData/",
            "schwung/luxr/kits."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Sounds",
          "lines": [
            "Each sound: 8 synth",
            "parameters (by its",
            "kind), the sample",
            "layer (sample,",
            "level,",
            "pitch, decay, start,",
            "tone, bend, synth",
            "level), level, pan,",
            "delay, reverb and",
            "drive sends, attack,",
            "gate, release, two",
            "LFOs synced to the",
            "tempo.",
            "Variation rolls the",
            "sound anew (0 = its",
            "factory sound)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "WAV layer",
          "lines": [
            "A sound's sample",
            "layer can play a WAV",
            "of your own:",
            "Page 5 > WAV File",
            "opens the sample",
            "browser (UserLibrary",
            "/Samples). Choosing",
            "a file sets Sample",
            "to WAV.",
            "",
            "Length:",
            "50 ms - its first 50",
            "ms, a transient, in",
            "the drum's envelope",
            "(like the LXR's).",
            "Whole - the whole",
            "file to its end,",
            "past the envelope.",
            "",
            "Pitch, Smp Decay,",
            "Start, Tone, Bend,",
            "Smp Lvl: on both.",
            "Up to 23 s at 44.1k,",
            "PCM 8-32 bit, float,",
            "mono or stereo."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Kit",
          "lines": [
            "Volume, Tune, Decay",
            "(all sounds), Output",
            "(+0/+3/+6 dB), Note",
            "Map, Tonal Snd, the",
            "master filter (- low",
            "pass, + high pass)",
            "and its resonance."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "FX",
          "lines": [
            "Drive & Reverb,",
            "Delay (tempo synced:",
            "1/8 to 3/4, mono,",
            "stereo, ping pong),",
            "Compressor, Limiter:",
            "as on LUXR."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "CPU",
          "lines": [
            "Setup > CPU: LUXR's",
            "share of the audio",
            "time in the last",
            "second, average and",
            "peak (100% = 2.9 ms,",
            "a whole block).",
            "Perform shows it at",
            "the bottom.",
            "",
            "A log line a second",
            "while it sounds:",
            "UserData/schwung/",
            "luxr/cpu.log"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
